RatesTest
├── isRatesStale
│   ├── given the cache has never been written
│   │   └── it is stale
│   ├── given the cache was written inside the window
│   │   └── it is fresh
│   ├── given the cache was written outside the window
│   │   └── it is stale
│   └── when a custom window is given
│       └── it uses that window instead of the default
├── rateAge
│   ├── given the currency has its own timestamp
│   │   └── it measures from that timestamp
│   ├── given the currency has no timestamp of its own
│   │   └── it falls back to the map-wide timestamp
│   ├── given neither timestamp exists
│   │   └── it reports an infinite age
│   └── when the currency is given in lower case
│       └── it matches the stored upper-case code
├── isCurrencyUsable
│   ├── given the currency is not in the map
│   │   └── it is not usable
│   ├── given the currency is younger than the hard cap
│   │   └── it is usable
│   └── given the currency is older than the hard cap
│       └── it is not usable
├── isRatesUsable
│   ├── given every currency is past the hard cap
│   │   └── it is not usable
│   ├── given one currency is still inside the cap
│   │   └── it is usable
│   └── given the map is empty
│       └── it is not usable
├── mergeRates
│   ├── given the incoming fetch covers only some currencies
│   │   ├── it keeps the currencies the fetch did not return
│   │   ├── it overwrites the currencies the fetch did return
│   │   └── it leaves the untouched currencies at their real age
│   ├── given an existing currency has no per-currency timestamp
│   │   └── it backfills from the map-wide timestamp
│   └── it takes the source and map-wide timestamp from the incoming fetch
└── stored values
    ├── given nothing has been stored
    │   ├── it reports empty rates
    │   ├── it reports no held rate
    │   └── it reports an idle fetch status
    ├── when rates are written
    │   ├── it reads them back
    │   └── it notifies watchers
    ├── when a held rate is written
    │   ├── it reads it back
    │   └── it notifies watchers
    └── when a fetch status is written
        ├── it records the state
        ├── it records the error
        └── it notifies watchers
